  "answer": "To study the presence of starch in leaves, you follow these steps: first, take a thin leaf from a plant exposed to sunlight. Then, boil the leaf in water to soften it. Next, transfer the leaf into a test tube with methylated spirit and boil it in a water bath. This removes the chlorophyll, making the leaf pale. After that, spread the leaf on a petridish and add a few drops of iodine solution. If starch is present, the leaf will turn bluish black.",
